# Deny by default, then let the static front end back in.
#
# This file is the only thing standing between `vercel deploy` and a public
# copy of certs/ca.key — the local CA's private key, which can mint a
# certificate any device that trusts it will accept — and data/turf.sqlite,
# which is the venue's real bookings and its password hashes. Neither is
# covered by .gitignore, because Vercel does not read .gitignore.
*

!index.html
!app.js
!styles.css
!client
!client/**

!mobile.html
!mobile.js
!mobile.css

!manifest.webmanifest
!icons
!icons/**

!vercel.json
